## 5. Architectural Anti-Patterns & Prohibitions

<div class="portal-alert-box">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">CRITICAL ANDROID VIOLATIONS</div>
  <p>Pull Requests containing any of the following anti-patterns will be automatically blocked by Danger CI:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Passing Context to ViewModels:</strong> Never pass <code>Context</code>, <code>Activity</code>, or <code>View</code> references into ViewModels. This causes severe memory leaks. Use AndroidViewModel strictly when Application context is required.</li>
    <li><strong>Exposing MutableStateFlow:</strong> ViewModels must always expose read-only <code>StateFlow&lt;UiState&gt;</code> via <code>_uiState.asStateFlow()</code>. UI composables must never mutate state directly.</li>
    <li><strong>Missing collectAsStateWithLifecycle:</strong> Using standard <code>collectAsState()</code> leaks coroutine resources when the app goes into the background. Always use <code>collectAsStateWithLifecycle()</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Compose Imports in ViewModels:</strong> ViewModels must remain completely framework-agnostic regarding UI rendering. Zero <code>androidx.compose.*</code> imports are allowed inside ViewModels.</li>
    <li><strong>Bypassing UseCases:</strong> ViewModels must never query repositories or Room DAOs directly. All data access must pass through a validated Use Case.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

